# The old addresses, kept working now that the documents are
# pages on this site. 302 rather than 301: a permanent redirect is cached
# in the browser for good, and these targets may yet move again.
#
# Never point a rule at a .html address. Pages serves /name from name.html
# and sends /name.html on to /name, so a rule /name -> /name.html bounces
# between the two for ever. The bare names below need no rule at all.
/bugs            /security               302
/docs            /documentation          302
/license         /licence                302
